WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.320
The Marvel Cinematic Universe&nbsp;
is getting godly in Phase 4.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:07.520
"Eternals," the 26th movie in the sprawling MCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:12.800
is hitting theaters in 2021, about a team&nbsp;
of heroes you may know nothing about. Here's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:17.120
everything you need to know about "Eternals,"&nbsp;
and how the film fits into Marvel's Phase 4.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.880
"You are about to meet the greatest&nbsp;
warriors the world has ever known."

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:26.480
"Eternals" was officially announced on&nbsp;
July 20, 2019 at Comic-Con in San Diego,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:31.200
with a slated premiere date of November&nbsp;
6, 2020. Unfortunately, when the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:37.040
coronavirus pandemic inevitably led to a total&nbsp;
reshuffling of the MCU slate, things changed.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:40.720
With theaters around the world shuttered,&nbsp;
"Black Widow" ultimately ended up being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:47.280
moved to May 2021, making 2020 the first&nbsp;
year without a Marvel movie since 2009.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:52.720
"Eternals" was given a new release date of&nbsp;
November 5, 2021. Fortunately, this schedule&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:57.680
actually stuck. Marvel fans have been hearing news&nbsp;
about a film based on the Eternals comics being in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:02.960
the works since the spring of 2018 — three and a&nbsp;
half years later, they'll finally get to see it.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:08.720
Even longtime Marvel fans might not be too&nbsp;
knowledgeable about who the Eternals are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:13.520
and their role in the Marvel Universe. After all,&nbsp;
they appeared in a relatively limited run of comic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:20.400
books in the mid 1970s and '80s. The storyline was&nbsp;
revived for a miniseries by Neil Gaiman in 2006,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:23.520
which brought these characters&nbsp;
into the modern Marvel universe.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:27.520
So, who are the Eternals, and what is their&nbsp;
significance? According to Marvel lore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:31.440
an alien species called the Celestials&nbsp;
visited Earth millions of years ago&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:34.960
and began carrying out experiments&nbsp;
on the inhabitants. Naturally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:38.720
the results of these experiments weren't&nbsp;
always a net positive for our planet.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:42.640
The Celestials were the original creators&nbsp;
of the Eternals, beings that looked like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:48.160
humans yet possessed abilities like flight, mind&nbsp;
reading, and unbelievable strength and endurance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:52.720
Their superpowers and resilience made them&nbsp;
essentially immortal and indestructible.

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:57.440
But the Celestials' experiments were also&nbsp;
responsible for the creation of the Deviants,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:02.080
another group of humanoids who were burdened&nbsp;
with genetic mutations and typically grotesque&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:06.720
in appearance. Humans mistook Eternals for&nbsp;
gods, and the Eternals often clashed with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:12.080
the Deviants to protect humanity. However, the&nbsp;
Eternals weren't unfailingly perfect — as we'll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:16.560
likely see in the film, they can be misled&nbsp;
and instigate conflicts among themselves.

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:22.560
At this point, we've met countless characters&nbsp;
from the original Marvel comics in the MCU.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:26.320
Have we been introduced to any&nbsp;
of the Eternals yet? Sort of.

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:30.560
It hasn't been mentioned in the movies yet,&nbsp;
but Thanos, the most formidable enemy of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:35.360
Avengers so far, was actually the child of&nbsp;
Eternals. If that seems a little confusing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:39.280
that's understandable — the Eternals&nbsp;
were supposed to be protecting humanity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:43.120
not wiping it out, and they should be&nbsp;
able to physically blend in among humans.

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:46.400
However, it's safe to say that&nbsp;
Thanos was a bit of a wild card,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:51.360
because he also possessed a recessive Deviant&nbsp;
gene, which explains his purply appearance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:55.680
Obviously lots of things can change in&nbsp;
the journey from the comics to the MCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.680 --> 00:03:00.080
so we wouldn't necessarily use him as an&nbsp;
example of the Eternals or Deviants to come.

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:03.520
Given that the MCU has never shied&nbsp;
away from streamlining or changing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:05.920
its characters' dense histories for the screen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:11.360
it's entirely possible that Thanos' comic history&nbsp;
as an Eternal-Deviant hybrid may not even come up.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:17.520
"Eternals" actually shares a connection with&nbsp;
another film in the MCU. In "Guardians of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:22.000
the Galaxy Vol. 2," Peter Quill's father,&nbsp;
Ego, tells Peter that he is a Celestial.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:27.920
"Celestial like a god?"
"Small 'g,' son."

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:34.240
He's portrayed as extremely powerful and possesses&nbsp;
god-like abilities. Ego is millions of years old,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:39.040
and he is able to manipulate the matter around&nbsp;
him. By the time we meet him in "Guardians Vol.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:44.560
2," he has managed to form a whole planet around&nbsp;
himself, but he can also inhabit a human body.

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:49.440
Yet all of this wasn't enough for Ego. He&nbsp;
eventually became bored with mere immortality and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:54.640
decided that he wanted to turn all of the worlds&nbsp;
in the cosmos into extensions of himself. But he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:59.520
wasn't capable of doing this alone, so he needed&nbsp;
another Celestial to help him turn his idea into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:04.480
reality. That's exactly why he became a father&nbsp;
in the first place — he hoped his son Peter would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:09.600
become his accomplice, and to ensure that his son&nbsp;
wouldn't be led astray, Ego killed Peter's mother.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:13.040
When Peter found out that Ego was&nbsp;
responsible for his mother's death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:18.000
he turned against Ego, and the Guardians teamed&nbsp;
up to destroy him. Clearly, the Celestials can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:22.240
have nefarious intentions, and they're not an&nbsp;
all-powerful force for good in the universe.

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:28.640
The cast of "Eternals" is rounded out with both&nbsp;
rising stars and A-listers. Richard Madden,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:31.280
who rose to fame for playing&nbsp;
the ill-fated Robb Stark in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:33.840
"Game of Thrones," has signed on to play Ikaris.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:38.240
Ikaris was known as the "Prime Eternal" in the&nbsp;
comics, meaning that he was more powerful than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:43.120
the other Eternals. He is fueled by cosmic energy,&nbsp;
and he can move at super speed and communicate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:48.320
telepathically. His sheer physical strength and&nbsp;
agility makes him a formidable opponent in combat.

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:51.400
"What is this even made of? Vibranium?"
"Don't-"

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:55.200
And speaking of "Game of Thrones," Kit Harington,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:59.520
who is best known for playing Jon Snow,&nbsp;
is in the "Eternals" cast as Dane Whitman.

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:04.160
Whitman isn't an Eternal himself, but he is&nbsp;
a superhero who goes by the name the Black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:08.000
Knight -- and it's likely that he'll have&nbsp;
a prominent place in future Marvel films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:11.520
one way or another. You may not have heard&nbsp;
of him, but it's worth mentioning that he's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:15.760
been a member of the Avengers -- and sometimes&nbsp;
even the team's leader -- for a very long time.

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:23.840
"Who do you think's gonna lead the Avengers?"
"I could lead them."

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:27.600
Ridloff was born Deaf, and as one&nbsp;
of the few Deaf actors in Hollywood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:31.360
she has always wanted to see more&nbsp;
representation for her community onscreen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:35.920
Now, she's made film history as the first&nbsp;
explicitly deaf superhero in the MCU.

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:40.320
Her casting also represents a major change&nbsp;
from the original comics — her character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:45.200
Makkari was actually a male character, and he&nbsp;
wasn't written as deaf. But the reception to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:49.840
this change has been overwhelmingly positive&nbsp;
so far, and fans are generally looking forward&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:54.240
to seeing Ridloff's portrayal of Makkari,&nbsp;
an Eternal with the power of super speed.

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:58.720
Angelina Jolie plays the ageless Eternal, Thena,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:02.720
in the "Eternals" cast — a major&nbsp;
get for the MCU, to say the least.

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:07.680
In the Marvel Universe, the city of Athens, Greece&nbsp;
was actually built for Thena, not the goddess&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:13.360
Athena as most would naturally assume. And that's&nbsp;
no inconsequential mix-up; human beings confusing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:18.560
Thena and Athena bred hostility between the&nbsp;
Eternals and the Olympic gods of Greek mythology,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:23.600
eventually leading to an all out war. In Gaiman's&nbsp;
"Eternals" comics, Thena works as a researcher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:28.640
at Stark Enterprises and starts remembering her&nbsp;
past as an Eternal through recurring nightmares.

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:32.160
Jolie is definitely the biggest name&nbsp;
attached to the "Eternals" cast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:37.600
and maybe the MCU in general, and she's ecstatic&nbsp;
to be part of the evolving on-screen universe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:40.000
Speaking at San Diego Comic-Con, she said,

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.360
"I'm going to work ten times harder.&nbsp;
I know what we all need to do,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:46.160
we have all read the script, we&nbsp;
all know what the task ahead is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:50.240
and we know what you deserve, so we are&nbsp;
all going to be working very, very hard."

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:55.200
When Marvel initially revealed the main&nbsp;
"Eternals" cast members at Comic-Con,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:58.720
they left audiences in suspense&nbsp;
about who would be playing Sersi.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:03.120
At Disney's D23 Expo it was announced&nbsp;
that Gemma Chan had landed the role.

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:08.720
As an Eternal, Sersi possesses powers like&nbsp;
transmutation, mind control, and flight. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:14.160
she also loves living among humans. She eventually&nbsp;
becomes a famous party planner in New York City,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:17.600
entertaining her guests with magic&nbsp;
that they believe is mere illusion.

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:23.040
Chan actually has a previous, unrelated role in&nbsp;
the MCU as the Kree warrior Minn-Erva, last seen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:27.520
getting blown up near the end of "Captain Marvel."&nbsp;
She's ecstatic to be joining the "Eternals"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:33.360
cast and having the opportunity to play a new&nbsp;
character in the MCU, posting on Twitter in 2019,

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:37.760
"I couldn't be happier to be coming back&nbsp;
to the MCU to play this iconic character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:40.000
and to work with this incredible group of people."

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:46.560
Chan isn't the only rising star joining the&nbsp;
"Eternals" cast. At D23, it was revealed that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:51.680
Barry Keoghan will officially be playing Druig.&nbsp;
Druig does have superpowers, but he doesn't use&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:56.240
them for good — he's the villain of the film,&nbsp;
wreaking havoc in the cosmos and on Earth.

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:59.600
Keoghan has wanted to join&nbsp;
the MCU for a while — in fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:03.440
he even tweeted to Stan Lee&nbsp;
about it in 2013, writing,

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:05.760
Stan Lee, Please Make me a SuperHero :).

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:07.760
Now, he's finally achieved his goal.

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:10.480
Keoghan caught the attention of&nbsp;
critics with his performance as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:13.440
George Mills in the Academy&nbsp;
Award-winning film "Dunkirk"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:17.600
and went on to star in the psychological&nbsp;
thriller "The Killing of a Sacred Deer."

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:22.720
Most recently, he played a role in two episodes of&nbsp;
the critically acclaimed HBO series "Chernobyl."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:26.560
Druig definitely represents a different&nbsp;
type of role for Keoghan, but clearly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:31.520
he's been waiting years for a shot at landing&nbsp;
a part in the MCU. Now, it's his time to shine.

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:36.560
Overall, the cast of "Eternals" is&nbsp;
stacked, with a few other names new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:39.280
to superherodom that you'll probably recognize.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.280 --> 00:08:44.560
Kumail Nanjiani will be playing Kingo, an&nbsp;
Eternal with a day job as a major Bollywood star.

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:47.280
Brian Tyree Henry will be appearing as Phastos,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:51.600
who basically develops all of the high-tech&nbsp;
gear and equipment that the Eternals need.
 &nbsp;

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:56.560
In an apparent first for Marvel, Lebanese actor&nbsp;
Haaz Sleiman will be appearing in "Eternals" as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.560 --> 00:09:01.520
Phastos' husband, making him one half of the&nbsp;
first openly gay relationship in the MCU.

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:06.640
Salma Hayek has signed on to play&nbsp;
Ajak, who often has to serve as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:10.400
diplomat between the Eternals and the&nbsp;
Celestials. This is because Ajak was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:14.640
originally the only Eternal with the ability&nbsp;
to directly communicate with the Celestials.

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:19.280
Don Lee is taking on the role of Gilgamesh, an&nbsp;
Eternal who in the comics has fought alongside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:23.920
the Avengers on numerous occasions, but&nbsp;
has been essentially overlooked until now.

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:28.720
Finally, Lia McHugh, the youngest member of&nbsp;
the main cast, is playing Sprite — as the name&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:32.560
suggests, she's a mischievous trickster whose&nbsp;
pranks have always gotten her into trouble.

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:36.560
Director Chloe Zhao will be&nbsp;
at the helm of "Eternals."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:38.640
Zhao is a newcomer to the world of Marvel.

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:42.320
These days, of course, Zhao is best&nbsp;
known as the director of "Nomadland."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:45.600
The film won three Academy&nbsp;
Awards, including Best Picture&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:50.560
and Best Director, making Zhao the second woman&nbsp;
in history to secure an Oscar for directing.

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:54.560
Zhao's history as an indie filmmaker turned&nbsp;
Oscar winner makes her an interesting choice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:58.400
for the director of Eternals. This film&nbsp;
definitely represents a new artistic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:03.840
direction for the filmmaker, but there's&nbsp;
no doubt that the movie is in good hands.

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:07.040
Young Syrian actor Zain Al&nbsp;
Rafeea has a supporting role&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:09.600
in "Eternals" -- and it may be a significant one.

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:12.880
While he only appears briefly in&nbsp;
the movie's teaser and trailer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:18.880
apparently as a prehistoric human, Salma Hayek&nbsp;
posted a photo with Lia McHugh and Al Rafeea,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:22.720
with the caption, "Hanging with the&nbsp;
Eternals' youth." Al Rafeea himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:27.520
hinted that he might be playing Namor the&nbsp;
Sub-Mariner, an Atlantean prince and mutant.

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:30.720
Time will tell whether or not these&nbsp;
rumors have any truth to them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:33.920
but if "Eternals" opens the door&nbsp;
to Marvel's undersea kingdom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:37.680
and the story of the first mutant,&nbsp;
it'll be even more of a must-see movie.

